    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79698" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παροιμ-ιάζω</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν
			Σαλομῶντα π</span>.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cite the Proverbs of</i> Solomon, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				4
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ma.</u>
				18.16
			</span></i> :—
				Med.
			, <i>make proverbial</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τὸν θεὸν πρῶτον παροιμιασάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					818b
				</span></i>
			 :— 
				Pass.
			, <i>pass into a proverb, become proverbial</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ -ιαζόμενος λόγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phlb.</u>
					45d
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ περὶ τῆς Αιβύης π</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				746b7
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ π. διὰ πικρότητα κόρχορος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>HP</u>
					7.7.2
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π</span>. <i>as the proverb
				goes</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.95
			</span></i> of; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥστε π. πρὸς προσποιουμένους</span>
			<i>it is proverbial</i> of pretenders, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				10.4.17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>speak in proverbs</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Hp.Ma.</u>
				301c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1129b29
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ παροιμιαζόμενοι</span>
			<i>people who quote proverbs</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				162c
			</span></i>.</div>
